<BaseLayout title="Terms of use | LearnNest" description="LearnNest terms of use for the demo site: sample data only, no real lessons, payments or accounts." path="/terms">
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: 22 November 2026. These terms are for the LearnNest demo site.</p>
  <h2>1. A demo site</h2>
  <p>LearnNest is a demonstration marketplace. Nothing on this site is a real offer to teach, learn, or sell a lesson. All tutor profiles, prices, ratings, reviews, student counts and lesson counts are sample figures.</p>
  <h2>2. No bookings, payments or accounts</h2>
  <p>Booking, application, enquiry and contact forms are demonstrations. Submitting a form sends nothing, books nothing, charges nothing, and creates no account.</p>
  <h2>3. No real tutors</h2>
  <p>Every tutor shown is a sample profile created for this demo. The names are invented and the initials-only avatars are coloured circles, not photos of real people.</p>
  <h2>4. Use of this site</h2>
  <p>You may browse LearnNest to see how a tutor marketplace works. You must not present the sample tutors as real people, copy the site’s content and present it as your own work, or use the site to mislead anyone into thinking a lesson has been booked or paid for.</p>
  <h2>5. No warranty</h2>
  <p>This demo is provided as it is, without any promise that it is complete, accurate or suitable for any purpose. If LearnNest becomes a real service, these terms will be replaced with full terms covering lessons, payments, cancellations and refunds.</p>
  <h2>6. Changes</h2>
  <p>These terms may change when the site changes. The date at the top of this page shows the latest version.</p>
</BaseLayout>
